Source Artifact <code>.glb</code>, <code>.gltf</code> <code>imported/&lt;path&gt;.amodel</code> the model as the engine uses it (<code>ModelFile</code>): vertex and index buffers compressed with meshoptimizer's lossless codecs (the geometry comes back bit for bit), the textures embedded as GPU-compressed KTX 2 files (below), the rest plain fields. Loads without a glTF parser or any image decoding <code>.slang</code> <code>imported/&lt;path&gt;.ashader</code> a shader module compiled ahead of time (<code>ShaderBundle</code>, Graphics): SPIR-V (Vulkan) and Metal shading language for each entry point, and the reflection, for the module without defines and for each <code>&lt;Variant&gt;</code> of its settings. A module with no <code>[shader(…)]</code> entry point (a library such as <code>common.slang</code>) is not an asset; it is a dependency of every shader that imports it, so editing it imports those shaders again <code>.png</code>, <code>.jpg</code>, <code>.jpeg</code> <code>imported/&lt;path&gt;.ktx2</code> a KTX 2 file with its whole mip chain: Basis Universal UASTC blocks (below), or with <code>compression="none"</code> 8-bit RGBA (<code>Ktx2Writer</code>). Either way the levels are supercompressed with zstd, which libktx inflates when it loads <p><code>imported/index.xml</code> says which source each artifact came from and which other files it was made from (a glTF's <code>.bin</code> and its textures):</p> <pre><code>&lt;Imports version="1"&gt;
  &lt;Import source="models/car.gltf" artifact="imported/models/car.gltf.amodel" key="9c1e…"&gt;
    &lt;Dependency path="models/car.bin"/&gt;
    &lt;Dependency path="models/wood.png"/&gt;
  &lt;/Import&gt;
&lt;/Imports&gt;
</code></pre> <p>An image that a model reads is part of that model and is not imported on its own. Files and folders whose name starts with a dot, and the <code>imported</code> folder itself, are never imported.</p>
